  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "4.0\n- Migrate One Call API from 2.5 (retired by OpenWeatherMap) to 4.0; requires a \"One Call by Call\" subscription for One Call API 4.0\n- Breaking: Remove GetWeatherOneCallAsync, GetWeatherOneCallHistoricAsync and OneCallOptions\n- Add GetWeatherOneCallCurrentAsync, GetWeatherOneCallMinutelyAsync, GetWeatherOneCall15MinutesAsync, GetWeatherOneCallHourlyAsync and GetWeatherOneCallDailyAsync (returning OneCallTimeline<T>)\n- Add GetWeatherOneCallNextPageAsync and GetWeatherOneCallPreviousPageAsync for timeline pagination\n- Add GetWeatherOneCallAlertAsync; weather records reference alerts by ID (Alerts)\n- Breaking: Rename HourlyWeatherForecast to TimelineWeatherForecast; AlertInfo follows the One Call API 4.0 format\n- Add Geocoding API: GetLocationsByNameAsync, GetLocationByZipCodeAsync, GetLocationsByCoordinatesAsync\n- Add GetAirPollutionForecastAsync and GetAirPollutionHistoryAsync\n- Breaking: UnitSystem.Standard returns temperatures in Kelvin (was Celsius)\n- Breaking: IOpenWeatherMapService has new members\n- Fix DailyWeatherForecastItem.Wind which was not deserialized\n- GetCurrentWeatherAsync validates latitude and longitude\n\n2.2\n- Maintenance updates\n- Replace Newtonsoft.Json with System.Text.Json\n- Change WeatherInfo.CityId from string to int\n- Mark GetWeatherOneCallAsync and GetWeatherOneCallHistoricAsync as obsolete (One Call API 2.5 was retired by OpenWeatherMap)\n\n2.1\n- Extended the 16-day forecast model (DailyWeatherForecastItem) with missing properties\n\n2.0\n- Use unit types from dependency UnitsNet\n\n1.2\n- Major refactoring in wind direction data model\n- Add multilingual support\n\n1.0\n- Initial release",
